# Guard for build-tarball's conditional patch application.
# Format: [!]<relpath-in-tarball>:<grep -E regex>   (ALL lines must hold)
# A leading '!' negates (the pattern must NOT be present).
#
# 0013 hooks the R1BIO_P2PDMA/R10BIO_P2PDMA tag sites that 0012 adds and
# fences legs through the meshstor advertise/observe machinery, so it needs
# exactly the tree shapes 0012 needs -- the same two predicates, for the
# same reasons (see 0012's guard for the full rationale). The el10-only
# activation is NOT the guard's job: that is compile-time, via
# MS_P2P_ROUTE_FENCE_KERNEL (HAVE_P2PDMA_PROVIDER && !HAVE_BLK_MQ_DMA_H)
# from compat/feature_flags.h, so one tarball still serves every kernel.
raid1-10.c:raid1_write_error
raid1-10.c:raid1_can_advertise_p2pdma
